Global Balance
\layout Itemize

Seek a stationary distribution through global balance equations.
 
\layout Itemize

At equilibrium the frequency of transitions out of state 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset 

 equals the frequency of transitions into 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset 

 
\begin_inset LatexCommand \citep[pg 260-262]{Bertsekas:data92}

\end_inset 

.
 
\layout Itemize

Markov chain can be defined by a transition probability matrix.
\begin_deeper 
\layout Itemize

Gives the probability of transition from any state to any other.
 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\mathbf{P}=\left[\begin{array}{ccccc}
P_{11} & \cdots & P_{i1} & \cdots & P_{N1}\\
\vdots & \ddots &  &  & \vdots\\
P_{1j} &  & P_{ij} &  & P_{Nj}\\
\vdots &  &  & \ddots & \vdots\\
P_{1N} & \cdots & P_{iN} & \cdots & P_{NN}\end{array}\right].\]

\end_inset 

where probability of transition from state 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset 

 to state 
\begin_inset Formula $j$
\end_inset 

 is given by 
\begin_inset Formula $P_{ij}$
\end_inset 

.
\end_deeper 
\layout ShortFoilhead

Global Balance II
\layout Itemize

If 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(j\right)$
\end_inset 

 is steady state probability for state 
\begin_inset Formula $j$
\end_inset 

, global balance says
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(j\right)\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}P_{ji}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}P\left(i\right)P_{ij}\]

\end_inset 

``the probability of leaving state 
\begin_inset Formula $j$
\end_inset 

 should be equal to the probability of arriving in state 
\begin_inset Formula $j$
\end_inset 

.''
\layout Itemize

Markov Process: rates of transfer.
 
\layout Itemize

Rates of transfer between states are given by a matrix with elements 
\begin_inset Formula $q_{ij}$
\end_inset 

 for transfer between 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset 

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $j$
\end_inset 

.
 Global balance equations give
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(j\right)\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}q_{ji}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}P\left(i\right)q_{ij}.\]

\end_inset 


\layout ShortFoilhead

Detailed Balance
\layout Itemize

For the birth death processes transitions only between state 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset 

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $k+1$
\end_inset 

 or 
\begin_inset Formula $k-1$
\end_inset 

.
 
\begin_deeper 
\layout Itemize


\begin_inset Formula $P_{ij}=0$
\end_inset 

 if 
\begin_inset Formula $i>j+1$
\end_inset 

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $i<j-1$
\end_inset 

.
 
\end_deeper 
\layout Itemize

Special case of the global balance: detailed balance equations.
 Looks at the flow between two states.
 
\layout Itemize

For the discrete case
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(k-1\right)P_{k-1,k}=P\left(k\right)P_{k,k-1}\]

\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

For the continuous case 
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(k-1\right)q_{k-1,k}=P\left(k\right)q_{k,k-1}.\]

\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

With our notation rate from 
\begin_inset Formula $q_{k-1,k}=\lambda_{k-1}$
\end_inset 

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $q_{k,k-1}=\mu_{k}$
\end_inset 

 giving
\layout Standard


\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(k-1\right)\lambda_{k-1}=P\left(k\right)\mu_{k}.\]

\end_inset 


\layout ShortFoilhead

