\layout Caption

Flow rates at a boundary for the 
\begin_inset Formula $M/M/1/m$
\end_inset 

 queue.
\begin_inset LatexCommand \label{cap:flowAtBoundaryMM1m}

\end_inset 


\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

At steady state, the expected flow from 
\begin_inset Formula $k-1$
\end_inset 

 to 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset 

 is given by 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda P\left(k-1\right)$
\end_inset 

.
 Flow from 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset 

 to 
\begin_inset Formula $k-1$
\end_inset 

 is given 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu P\left(k-1\right)$
\end_inset 

.
 For flow to be balanced we have 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\lambda P\left(k-1\right)=\mu P\left(k\right)\]

\end_inset 

 leading to 
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(k\right)=\frac{\lambda}{\mu}P\left(k-1\right).\]

\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

Substituting into the detailed balance equation we get
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(k\right)=\frac{\lambda}{\mu}P\left(k-1\right)\]

\end_inset 

 Thus 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
P\left(k\right) & = & \left(\frac{\lambda}{\mu}\right)^{k}\\
P\left(0\right) & = & \rho^{k}P\left(0\right).\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

 
\layout ShortFoilhead

Normalisation
\layout Itemize

In the case of the finite length queue the normalisation is computed with
 a sum over only 
\begin_inset Formula $m$
\end_inset 

 states, rather than 
\begin_inset Formula $\infty$
\end_inset 

 states.
 This leads to a different value for 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(0\right)$
\end_inset 

.
 We compute 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(0\right)$
\end_inset 

 by writing the sum across all the 
\begin_inset Formula $m+1$
\end_inset 

 states of the distribution, 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\sum_{k=0}^{m}P\left(0\right)\rho^{k}=1.\]

\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

This leads us to 
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(0\right)=\sum_{k=0}^{m}\frac{1}{\rho^{k}}\]

\end_inset 

which is recognised as the 
\emph on 
finite 
\emph default 
sum of a geometric series,
\begin_inset Formula \[
\sum_{k=0}^{m}\frac{1}{\rho^{k}}=\frac{1-\rho}{1-\rho^{m+1}}\]

\end_inset 

so we have
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(0\right)=\frac{1-\rho}{1-\rho^{m+1}}\]

\end_inset 

which leads to 
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(k\right)=\frac{\rho^{k}\left(1-\rho\right)}{1-\rho^{m+1}}.\]

\end_inset 


\layout ShortFoilhead

